ArchiveEntry "Sign assembly: nonneg-weighted sum of nonpositive terms is nonpositive (4 terms)"

/* Abstract building block for the 4-corner box-descent decomposition.
 * If weights wA..wD >= 0, corner values nA..nD <= 0, and V = sum wI*nI, then V<=0.
 * Proven over scalar variables (trivial QE) so it can be INSTANTIATED with the
 * explicit (big) polynomials by substitution -- avoiding Z3 re-expanding them. */

ProgramVariables
  Real wA; Real wB; Real wC; Real wD;
  Real nA; Real nB; Real nC; Real nD; Real VV;
End.

Problem
  \forall wA \forall wB \forall wC \forall wD \forall nA \forall nB \forall nC \forall nD \forall VV (
    ( wA>=0 & wB>=0 & wC>=0 & wD>=0 & nA<=0 & nB<=0 & nC<=0 & nD<=0 &
      VV = wA*nA + wB*nB + wC*nC + wD*nD )
    -> VV <= 0 )
End.

Tactic "Proof"
  QE
End.

End.
